  _isSmallIngredient: 0
  _recipeBookDescriptionUnspoiled: 
  _recipeBookDescriptionSpoiled: A warm spinach pie was a common treat accompanied
    by a grandmother's glowing smile and a cup of warm milk, as she regaled folk
    stories next to the hearth. However, with spinach and other fresh greens now
    a luxury, since fresh produce despise the little patches of toxic dirt left in
    Verehn, the creamy and savory spinach pie seems as distant as Babushka's resting
    place. Nevertheless, the people now must make do with what they have. If you
    squint hard enough, the green streaks of mold in the half-melted cheese do look
    like spinach, no? Just think back to that simpler time, beside your beloved grandmother,
    then sully that memory with this 'spinach' pie.
